.TH OKFSMITH 1 "October 2026" "okfsmith 0.7.7" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
okfsmith \- forge messy documents into OKF v0.2 knowledge bundles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B okfsmith
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B okfsmith
is a Python CLI that ingests messy documents (PDFs, markdown, wiki dumps,
Notion exports) and emits spec-conformant OKF v0.2 knowledge bundles:
markdown files with YAML frontmatter, plus reserved
.B index.md
and
.B log.md
files. Every concept carries provenance
.RI ( sources[] ),
a trust tier, and lifecycle metadata, and every bundle is checked by a
built-in \(sc11 validator. The bundle is always the first positional
argument.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init \fIBUNDLE\fR [\-\-force] [\-\-yes]
Scaffold
.B index.md
and
.B log.md
in
.IR BUNDLE .
Refuses a non-empty directory unless
.B \-\-force
is given (asks for confirmation unless
.BR \-\-yes ).
.TP
.B ingest \fIBUNDLE\fR \fISOURCE\fR... [\-\-recursive] [\-\-no\-llm] [\-\-model \fINAME\fR] [\-\-provider \fINAME\fR] [\-\-api\-base \fIURL\fR] [\-\-api\-key \fIKEY\fR] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-quiet]
Parse, section, and extract each
.I SOURCE
(file or directory) into draft concepts. Sources are SHA-256 fingerprinted:
already-ingested files are skipped.
.B \-\-no\-llm
writes one draft concept per section, fully offline.
.TP
.B sync \fIBUNDLE\fR \fISOURCE\fR... [\-\-recursive] [\-\-no\-llm] [\-\-model \fINAME\fR] [\-\-provider \fINAME\fR] [\-\-api\-base \fIURL\fR] [\-\-api\-key \fIKEY\fR] [\-\-watch] [\-\-interval \fISECONDS\fR] [\-\-poll] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-quiet] [\-\-format text|json]
Incrementally sync the bundle with its sources: each file is SHA-256
fingerprinted and only new, changed, renamed, or deleted files are
processed. Changed files have their concepts replaced (never duplicated);
renamed files keep their concepts; deleted files have their concepts
removed. Additions are applied before deletions. State lives in
.IBUNDLE /.okfsmith/sync-state.json
and interrupted runs resume cleanly.
.B \-\-watch
re-scans on a timer (Ctrl-C stops);
.B \-\-dry\-run
reports without writing.
.TP
.B validate \fIBUNDLE\fR [\-\-format text|json] [\-\-strict]
Check OKF \(sc11 conformance. Exit 0 means conformant.
.B \-\-strict
also fails on warnings.
.TP
.B list \fIBUNDLE\fR [\-\-format text|json] [\-\-tier \fITIER\fR]
List concepts, optionally filtered by trust tier
.RI ( unverified ,
.IR machine-confirmed ,
.IR human-reviewed ).
The text table's
.B Valid
column shows the temporal status of each concept
.RB ( \(em
for concepts without temporal frontmatter, otherwise
.IR current ,
.IR expired ,
.IR future ,
or
.IR superseded );
JSON output adds
.IR temporal_status .
.TP
.B read \fIBUNDLE\fR \fICONCEPT_ID\fR [\-\-format text|json]
Print one concept (id is the bundle-relative path without
.BR .md ).
Concepts carrying temporal frontmatter
.RB ( valid_from ,
.BR valid_until ,
.BR supersedes ,
.BR last_verified )
or superseded by another concept print a one-line
.I [temporal: ...]
badge after the body; JSON output adds
.IR temporal_status .
.TP
.B graph \fIBUNDLE\fR [\-\-format text|json|mermaid|html] [\-\-output \fIFILE\fR]
Show concept links. The
.B html
format writes a self-contained offline viewer
.RI ( viz.html ).
.TP
.B mcp \fIBUNDLE\fR [\-\-transport stdio|sse|streamable\-http]
Serve the bundle to AI agents over MCP. Requires the
.B mcp
extra.
.TP
.B doctor
Check dependencies, optional extras, Ollama reachability, temp-dir
writability, and the resolved LLM backend (provider, base URL, model,
key status — the key itself is never shown).
.TP
.B chat \\fR[\\fIBUNDLE\\fR] [\\-\\-model \\fINAME\\fR] [\\-\\-provider \\fINAME\\fR] [\\-\\-api\\-base \\fIURL\\fR] [\\-\\-api\\-key \\fIKEY\\fR] [\\-\\-no\\-llm]
Interactive Q&A over the bundle (REPL): plain-language questions answered
with concept-id citations, plus slash commands
.RI ( /help ,
/ingest, /list, /read, /search, /validate, /graph, /doctor, /model, /clear,
/exit ).
Generative answers via Ollama, any \-\-provider preset
.RI ( openrouter ,
groq, mistral, deepseek, together, fireworks, deepinfra, anyscale,
perplexity, xai, gemini, openai, agentrouter, lmstudio), or a custom
\-\-api\-base endpoint;
falls back to extractive mode when no LLM is reachable.
Anthropic's native API is not OpenAI-compatible: use the
.B openrouter
preset or a compat proxy via
.BR \-\-api\-base .
.TP
.B eval \fIBUNDLE\fR [\-\-init\-sample] [\-\-top\-k \fIN\fR] [\-\-fail\-under \fIPCT\fR] [\-\-metric\-threshold \fIT\fR] [\-\-as\-of \fIDATE\fR] [\-\-include\-superseded] [\-\-no\-llm] [\-\-model \fINAME\fR] [\-\-provider \fINAME\fR] [\-\-api\-base \fIURL\fR] [\-\-api\-key \fIKEY\fR] [\-\-format text|json]
Score the bundle against its golden Q&A set
.RI ( <bundle>/eval/golden.json ;
\-\-init\-sample writes a starter set).
Each question is answered with the shared BM25 engine (same ranking as
search, chat, and MCP, including temporal supersession hiding) and scored
on context relevancy, faithfulness, and answer relevancy; every score is
labeled heuristic (keyless) or llm-judge, and failing questions are
diagnosed as retrieval vs generation failures.
.B \-\-fail\-under
gates CI: exit 1 when the overall score (0\-100) misses it.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (for
.BR validate :
conformant).
.TP
.B 1
Expected failure; the message starts with
.BR "error [CODE]:" ,
e.g.
.BR "error [bundle-not-found]:" ,
and includes a hint. No tracebacks.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (bad flags, invalid enum choices, conflicting options).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OKFSMITH_MODEL
Default model name for LLM extraction.
.TP
.B OKFSMITH_PROVIDER
Provider preset name (e.g.
.BR openrouter ).
.TP
.B OKFSMITH_API_KEY
API key for the configured endpoint; preferred over
.BR \-\-api\-key ,
which lands in shell history (never read from files, never displayed).
.TP
.B OKFSMITH_API_BASE
Custom OpenAI-compatible base URL (full base, e.g.
.IR https://my-proxy/v1 ).
.TP
.B OPENAI_API_KEY
API key for OpenAI-compatible backends (never read from files).
.TP
.B OKFSMITH_BASE_URL
Base URL for OpenAI-compatible backends.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I completions/okfsmith.bash
.TQ
.I completions/okfsmith.zsh
.TQ
.I completions/okfsmith.fish
Shell completion scripts (source from your shell rc file, or run
.BR "okfsmith --install-completion" ).
